# Módulos NestJS

Detalhe: `docs/02-module-anatomy.md`

## Anatomia

```
src/modules/{entity}/
  {entity}.module.ts
  controllers/{action}-{entity}.controller.ts
  services/{action}-{entity}.service.ts
  repositories/{entity}.repository.ts
  repositories/prisma-{entity}.repository.ts
  repositories/@types.ts
  dtos/entity/{entity}.entity.ts
  dtos/request/{action}-{entity}.dto.ts
  dtos/response/{action}-{entity}.dto.ts
```

## Naming

| Ação | Controller | Service | Rota |
|------|------------|---------|------|
| create | `CreateProductController` | `CreateProductService` | `POST /products` |
| get | `GetProductController` | `GetProductService` | `GET /products/:id` |
| fetch | `FetchProductsController` | `FetchProductsService` | `GET /products` |
| update | `UpdateProductController` | `UpdateProductService` | `PUT /products/:id` |
| delete | `DeleteProductController` | `DeleteProductService` | `DELETE /products/:id` |

- Rotas: plural, kebab-case (`/cost-centers`, `/unit-of-measurements`).
- Catálogo e lançamentos: `@FarmScoped()` na classe; `@FarmId()` / `@OrganizationId()` nos params — **não** `@UsePipes` no método (validaria o contexto de tenancy como body).
- Service: um método público `execute(...)`; lança exceções Nest (`NotFoundException`, etc.).

## Repository

```typescript
// product.repository.ts
export interface ProductRepository { /* ... */ }
export const PRODUCT_REPOSITORY = 'PRODUCT_REPOSITORY';

// product.module.ts
providers: [
  { provide: PRODUCT_REPOSITORY, useClass: PrismaProductRepository },
  CreateProductService,
],
exports: [PRODUCT_REPOSITORY], // se outro módulo precisa
```

- Injetar via `@Inject(PRODUCT_REPOSITORY)` — não `PrismaService` direto no service de use case.
- Cross-módulo: importar o módulo e usar o token exportado (ex.: `UnitOfMeasurementModule` em `ProductModule`).
